{"availability":"available","full":"at0m-b0mb/AirMouse-Hand-Gesture-Control","name":"AirMouse-Hand-Gesture-Control","description":"A Python-based Air Mouse using hand gestures to control the mouse. The project utilizes OpenCV, MediaPipe, and Autopy libraries to track hand movements, allowing users to perform mouse actions with simple gestures. This repository includes two versions: a standalone Air Mouse and a Client-Server architecture that enables remote mouse control.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2024-10-08T19:00:54Z","updated":"2026-10-03T01:27:26Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://at0m-b0mb.github.io/AirMouse-Hand-Gesture-Control/","topics":["computer-vision","gesture-control","mediapipe","opencv","python"],"demo":"https://at0m-b0mb.github.io/AirMouse-Hand-Gesture-Control/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T23:49:36.578Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T23:49:36.578Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T23:49:36.578Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T15:37:51.414Z","stars":3,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-12T23:49:36.578Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Control your laptop entirely in the air — cursor, clicks, scroll, drag & type.","No touch needed. Just your hand and a webcam."],"features":["One Euro Filter — smooth when still, instant when you move. No lag, no jitter.","Left, right, middle (opt-in), and double-click — all with pinch hysteresis.","Peace sign → move hand up/down/left/right. Optional inertia/momentum glide.","Fist to grab, open hand to drop. Works across monitors.","Hold open palm to toggle. QWERTY + function row + Caps/Shift + live text preview."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/at0m-b0mb/AirMouse-Hand-Gesture-Control/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f3bb6c95dd292a4386ff680efb4a37adbf8b08b3413c521fdfcf333afcc02fde","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T15:37:51.595Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:3